From: chelovechishee <261262090+chelovechishee@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH 38/53] power: supply: s2m-charger: unmask the MUIC interrupt
 output

S-Boot leaves INT_MASK set in MUIC CTRL1, as the vendor MUIC driver
clears it at probe and we have none on boards without a MUIC node. The
attach status then latches but never raises the interrupt: with VBUS
read 100 ms after it comes, before BC1.2 is done, a dedicated charger
plugged in after boot stayed "Unknown" at 500 mA.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/power/supply/s2m-charger.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/s2m-charger.c b/drivers/power/supply/s2m-charger.c
index c0bbaace4..8f453284d 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/s2m-charger.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/s2m-charger.c
@@ -337,6 +337,13 @@ static int s2mu005_chgr_probe_standalone(struct s2m_chgr *priv,
 					     irqs[i]);
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * The bootloader leaves the MUIC's interrupt output masked: attach,
+	 * which comes when BC1.2 has found a dedicated charger, would then only
+	 * be read along with a VBUS interrupt, and that one comes before it.
+	 */
+	regmap_clear_bits(priv->regmap, S2MU005_REG_MUIC_CTRL1, S2MU005_MUIC_IRQ);
+
 	schedule_delayed_work(&priv->detect_work, 0);
 
 	return 0;
-- 
